<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swabia (Bavaria)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bavarian Swabia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a> is an administrative region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, often called Bavarian Swabia, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a>. It covers the Swabian lands between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iller">Iller</a> and the Lech, including Augsburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kempten">Kempten</a> and Memmingen, which the Kingdom of Bavaria acquired in 1803–1810 from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/free-imperial-city">free cities</a>, prince-bishoprics and other territories. Its people speak Swabian dialects of Alemannic German.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swabia-bavaria.jpg" alt="Swabia (Bavaria)" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zebra848 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Schwaben_Bayern.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
